<http://data.silknow.org/object/94661480-2b5f-352d-b7ee-183a21f9fd56>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Shirt, silk, Greece (Crete) around 1851-1876."@en , "Man's shirt of woven, natural raw silk with two warp stripes of a heavier degummed silk thread at each selvage. The shirt is made up in the traditional Cretan manner, using only unshaped loom widths of material. Front andback are formed of one width without shoulder seams. The upper part of each sleeve consists of one width, and a single strip one width wide runs from wrist to hem, forming the under part of the sleeve and the sides of the garment. Hems and neck edge are hand-rolled and finished with button holing. The wrists have a narrow edging of bibila lace with small leaves. The low V neck has an inch of embroidery in an insertion stitch to strengthen the V.\n\nThe front and back are formed of one width without shoulder seams. \n\nThe upper part of each sleeve consists of one width and a single strip, one width wide, runs from wrist to hem, forming the under part of the sleeve and the sides of the garment. \n\nThe hems and neck edge are hand rolled and finished with buttonholing. \n\nThe wrists have a narrow edging of bibila lace with small leaves. \n\nThe low V neck has an inch of embroidery in an insertion stitch to strengthen the V."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ddde0767-06c3-3888-8db0-8f33d6369f5a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/398e72bd-3006-3a4a-92a0-f78c156cc6fc> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Shirt, silk, Greece (Crete) around 1851-1876."@en , "Man's shirt of woven, natural raw silk with two warp stripes of a heavier degummed silk thread at each selvage. The shirt is made up in the traditional Cretan manner, using only unshaped loom widths of material. Front andback are formed of one width without shoulder seams. The upper part of each sleeve consists of one width, and a single strip one width wide runs from wrist to hem, forming the under part of the sleeve and the sides of the garment. Hems and neck edge are hand-rolled and finished with button holing. The wrists have a narrow edging of bibila lace with small leaves. The low V neck has an inch of embroidery in an insertion stitch to strengthen the V.\n\nThe front and back are formed of one width without shoulder seams. \n\nThe upper part of each sleeve consists of one width and a single strip, one width wide, runs from wrist to hem, forming the under part of the sleeve and the sides of the garment. \n\nThe hems and neck edge are hand rolled and finished with buttonholing. \n\nThe wrists have a narrow edging of bibila lace with small leaves. \n\nThe low V neck has an inch of embroidery in an insertion stitch to strengthen the V."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/94661480-2b5f-352d-b7ee-183a21f9fd56/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/94661480-2b5f-352d-b7ee-183a21f9fd56/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/94661480-2b5f-352d-b7ee-183a21f9fd56/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/94661480-2b5f-352d-b7ee-183a21f9fd56/dimension/3> ;
